        {
         "id": "n1",
         "value": "<b>Design notes</b><br/>&#8226; W5500 sits on <b>spi2</b> (PB13/14/15, CS PB12, RST PB11) because DCMI hard-owns PA4 (VSYNC) and PA6 (PIXCLK) with no remap available.<br/>&#8226; STM32F4 DCMI has <b>no CGR/CCMR</b>, so chroma is stripped on the CPU; BSM/OEBS at CR 16-18 are reserved per RM0090.<br/>&#8226; The OV7670 has <b>no YUV420</b> mode - 8-bit outputs are YUV422 / RGB / GRB 4:2:2 / Raw - so QVGA YUV422 (153600 B) cannot fit 128 KB RAM.<br/>&#8226; Socket 0 = micro-ROS, socket 1 = video. Every cross-container edge runs in a gutter between containers; edges inside one container run in the gaps between boxes.<br/>&#8226; Parallel edges are held at least 24 px apart so individual lines stay traceable.<br/>&#8226; Tests: renode-test robot suite plus the standalone W5500 model project.",
         "style": "rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;align=left;",
         "parent": "1",
         "vertex": "1",
         "geometry": {
          "x": 40,
          "y": 1180,
          "width": 1880,
          "height": 140
         }
        },
